## Epigraph

<!-- page 5: 2 nuggets -->

> "More is learned from one's errors than from one's successes."
> — Primo Levi

> "I must create a system or be enslaved by another man's."
> — William Blake

- [MUST KNOW][N001] These two epigraphs frame the entire book: trading mastery
  comes from analyzing your failures (Levi), and the only viable path is an
  original, personally-owned methodology (Blake). Following someone else's
  system keeps you permanently dependent and unable to adapt.

